WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:06.000
Very well. Everything that needed to be said has been spoken.

00:06.560 --> 00:13.700
Your Highness need not rush to agree. Wan'er judges a man by his actions, not his words.

00:14.160 --> 00:19.500
What I overheard is that tonight, this batch of embezzled grain will be ferried away by boat.

00:20.080 --> 00:23.600
Whether to act or not rests entirely with Your Highness.

00:42.680 --> 00:46.800
Your Highness, I took scouts there—that location indeed hides a secret storehouse!

00:47.440 --> 00:53.600
Peering from a distance, I saw them actively transferring provisions. I fear after tonight, that depot will be gone!

00:55.080 --> 00:57.120
Your Highness, let us dispatch troops at once!

00:57.240 --> 00:59.500
Without an imperial warrant, where would we mobilize soldiers?

00:59.720 --> 01:04.200
The capital garrison! They are my sworn brothers of life and death—no tally is required!

01:05.480 --> 01:07.960
Just give the word, and I shall lead them out immediately!

01:08.000 --> 01:13.000
Mobilizing imperial troops without authorization is a capital treason offense—especially the capital garrison!

01:15.720 --> 01:24.000
If our proof is ironclad, His Majesty will surely show clemency once we explain everything posthaste and reduce the matter to a minor infraction!

01:24.360 --> 01:28.000
At worst, he will merely strip me of my military post!

01:29.080 --> 01:31.000
Your Highness, this opportunity will never come again!
